(FIL-75: Delete the file "<path>" removes the file; deleting a file that is not there sets the error flag.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-75.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   doomed.txt exists before the delete
   doomed.txt is gone after the delete
   deleting a missing file set the error flag
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/doomed.txt".
Write "temporary" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
If "vf_scratch/files/doomed.txt" is available then,
    print "doomed.txt exists before the delete".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/files/doomed.txt".
On error print "the delete set the error flag".
If "vf_scratch/files/doomed.txt" is not available then,
    print "doomed.txt is gone after the delete".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/files/doomed.txt".
On error print "deleting a missing file set the error flag".
